  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The sequence \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\log_{12} 162, \\ \\log_{12} x, \\ \\log_{12} y, \\\\ \\ \\log_{12} z, \\ \\log_{12} 1250 \\end{gathered} \\] is an arithmetic progression. What is \\(x?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(125\\sqrt{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(270\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(162\\sqrt{5}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(434\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(225\\sqrt{6}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "270"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2013-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because the logarithms are in arithmetic progression, \\(162, x, y, z, 1250\\) is a geometric sequence. Its common ratio \\(r\\) satisfies \\(162 r^4 = 1250,\\) so \\(r^4 = \\tfrac{625}{81}\\) and \\(r = \\tfrac53.\\)\n\nTherefore \\(x = 162\\cdot\\tfrac53 = 270.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Equal differences of logs mean \\(162, x, y, z, 1250\\) is a geometric sequence",
        "Find the common ratio \\(r\\) from \\(162r^4 = 1250\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
